=== task 2.2: tests/test_modctx_pin.c pins the bound [0, K) of adf_modctx_recombine ===

The line of the library: src/modctx.c:603, `fmpz_fdiv_r(out, out, ctx->K);` in
adf_modctx_recombine, which is the line that carries the range [0, K) of src/modctx_internal.h.

green (clean tree):
  $ make build/test_modctx_pin && ./build/test_modctx_pin
  7 tests, 5716 checks, 0 failed checks, 0 failed tests
  exit 0, real 0m0,008s

red (scratch copy build/scratch/pin, the bound moved by one: line 603 kept and
     "    fmpz_add_ui(out, out, 1);" added after it, so the range becomes (0, K]):
  $ ./build/test_modctx_pin ; echo $?
  1
  (first lines of the run)
  FAIL tests/test_modctx_pin.c:137: every_residue_of_K_35_is_the_representative_in_0_K: fmpz_equal(out, want)
       | out = 1, the oracle says 0, for the residues (0, 0)
  FAIL tests/test_modctx_pin.c:137: ... out = 16, the oracle says 15, for the residues (0, 1)
  ...
  7 tests, 5716 checks, 2847 failed checks, 7 failed tests
  The old pin of the same bound, tests/test_modctx_limits.c, on the same scratch build:
  $ ./build/test_modctx_limits ; echo $?
  1
  7 tests, 239 checks, 76 failed checks, 1 failed tests

second red case (the line deleted, not moved), the case the closure judge named
(lanes/m1-closure-contexts/report.md:133-134):
  $ sed -i '604d' src/modctx.c && make -j2 build/test_modctx_pin build/test_modctx_limits
  $ ./build/test_modctx_pin
  7 tests, 5716 checks, 0 failed checks, 0 failed tests
  $ ./build/test_modctx_limits
  7 tests, 239 checks, 0 failed checks, 0 failed tests
  So the new pin fails when the bound is moved and, like the old one, does not fail when the
  line is only deleted: on FLINT 3.0.1 fmpz_multi_CRT_precomp(..., 0) returns a value of [0, K)
  by itself, and no test of the value can see the difference. This is stated, not hidden.

